  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CDMu Sustainable Agriculture Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(i)	To provide funds, training, agricultural and management inputs to farmers that will allow poor and marginalized persons (mainly female headed households) to carry out sustainable agriculture. Production of a variety of crops will help each beneficiary household to improve its nutrition while surplus yields will be sold to earn some cash income.

(ii)	To provide credit for business, training and management of crop husbandry to poor farmers, particularly women. This will help to improve and increase food production and will address food insecurity.

(iii)	To provide credit for the purchase of water pumps in order to promote micro-irrigation in some parts of Maragua District. This will help to increase food production, improve household income and food security.

(iv)	To restore and maintain the fertility of soils on participating farms by engaging in soil conservation and water retention activities

(v)	To assist some farmers to add value to primary products and engage in small-scale agro-enterprise.

(vi)	To develop the capability of the Diocese Development Office (DDO) by improving staff capacities in order to help meet the programme planning, implementation and management challenges of the Diocese now and in the years to come.

(vii)	To equip the development office with one vehicle, two motor cycles and basic office equipment.</narrative>
  </description>
